{"id":"word:hebrew:H589","type":"word","title":"אֲנִי","subtitle":"H589 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"I","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֲנִי (H589) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: p.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 874 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֲנִי (ʼănîy) means I First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֲנִי","transliteration":"ʼănîy","pronunciation":"an-ee'","strong":"H589","lemmaId":"hebrew:H589","partOfSpeech":"p","forms":["אֲנִ֥י","אֲנִ֣י","אֲנִ֖י","אֲנִי֙","אֲנִ֤י"],"morphs":[["HPp1cs",693],["HC/Pp1cs",178],["HTr/Pp1cs",2],["HTi/Pp1cs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"I","usage":"I, (as for) me, mine, myself, we, × which, × who.","full":"H589. ani אָ֫נִי אֲנִי, pronoun 1 singular, common I (, אֲנָא , , ) Gen 6:17 ; 9:9 , 12 + often Following a participle as its subject (to express mostly either a true present or the futurum instans [immanent future]) 18:17 אֲנִי הַמְכַסֶּה Amos I hiding from Abraham that which, etc., Judg 15:3 ; 1Sam 3:13 Jer 1:12 ; 38:14 ; 44:29 (see Dr § 135, 4 ). Appended to a verb, it expresses, in early Hebrew, a real emphasis, as Judg 8:23 בָּכֶם אֲנִי אֶמְשֹׁל לֹא I will not rule over you, 2Sam 12:28 lest I take the city, 17:15 thus and thus did Ahitophel counsel, and thus and thus אָ֫נִי יָעַצְתִּי did I counsel; but in later Hebrew It is sometimes pelonastc, Eccl 2:11 , 15 , 18 , 20 +. In response to a question, אָ֫נִי alone = I am, It is I , Gen 27:24 ; Judg 13:11 ; 1Kin 18:8 +. With הַאֲנִי הֲֶ Isa 66:9 . (Synonym אָנֹכִּי , q. v.)","rootNote":"contracted from 595 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 7","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 7","1Chr 17 13","1Chr 17 16","1Chr 21 10","1Chr 21 17","1Chr 21 17","1Chr 22 7","1Chr 22 10"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenc